## Task
Implement the main TabView with NavigationStack per tab and router path management.

## Why This Matters
The tab bar is the primary navigation paradigm. Each tab needs its own navigation stack to maintain back button state independently.

## Tab Structure (3 Tabs)
1. **Library** - Book grid/list with search bar at top (search is inline, not a separate tab)
2. **Capture** - Camera for capturing book covers and quote pages
3. **Settings** - Configuration, API key management, marking definitions

**Note:** Search is accessed via a search bar within LibraryView, not as a separate tab. This keeps the tab bar simple and follows iOS conventions (search within context).

## Implementation Details

### ContentView with TabView
```swift
struct ContentView: View {
    @State private var selectedTab: Tab = .library

    var body: some View {
        TabView(selection: $selectedTab) {
            LibraryTab()
                .tabItem { Label("Library", systemImage: "books.vertical") }
                .tag(Tab.library)

            CaptureTab()
                .tabItem { Label("Capture", systemImage: "camera") }
                .tag(Tab.capture)

            SettingsTab()
                .tabItem { Label("Settings", systemImage: "gear") }
                .tag(Tab.settings)
        }
    }
}

enum Tab: Hashable {
    case library
    case capture
    case settings
}
```

### Each Tab Wraps a NavigationStack
```swift
struct LibraryTab: View {
    @State private var router = RouterPath()

    var body: some View {
        NavigationStack(path: $router.path) {
            LibraryView()
                .navigationDestination(for: Book.self) { book in
                    BookDetailView(book: book)
                }
                .navigationDestination(for: Quote.self) { quote in
                    QuoteDetailView(quote: quote)
                }
        }
        .environment(router)
    }
}
```

### RouterPath Pattern
```swift
@Observable
class RouterPath {
    var path = NavigationPath()

    func navigate(to destination: any Hashable) {
        path.append(destination)
    }

    func pop() {
        if !path.isEmpty {
            path.removeLast()
        }
    }

    func popToRoot() {
        path = NavigationPath()
    }
}
```

